module contract;

// Card CELL-GUARD-RESULT-RANGE-CHECKED (contract specification C09.4, grammar
// G05j, gateway rule 38e). USER DECISION 2026-11-03 (verbatim): "C: a new
// result-set form that allows unions, such as result_set(-1 | [0, MAX]). It
// is the only option that can also state open's and timerfd_create's results
// (needed by RULE-38-VALIDITY-READING-RESULT-SET). It is also the largest
// grammar change. I choose this because we must not loosen the custody of
// the contracts if we cannot select other options."
//
// The C library's documented result sets, as bounds contract v1 result sets.
// Each declaration is a VALUE SET ONLY: it states which integers the call
// returns and nothing about custody. It is not a resource declaration: it
// neither creates, releases, transfers nor borrows anything, so `pipe` stays
// undeclared for custody (`unistd.qv`: a descriptor has no out slot in that
// vocabulary) and `open`'s resource v1 declaration in `unistd.qv` is
// unchanged; this module's `open` stands beside it and adds no custody
// (relation `null_deref_beside`). The resource loader rejects this module and
// the bounds consumer never reads a result set (`for_bounds`).
//
// Every declaration is `requires bounds_revision(flexible);`: it binds by
// name and declared signature at any revision of the audited project (C06.2's
// flexible mode), under the one standing libc assumption
// `libc-c-standard-abi`; no libc body is analysed. Which C library is in use
// is the build's provenance. The set is read only while the declaration is in
// force (not held, not withdrawn, the call bound to the C library's function:
// no analysed body of the same name); a set out of force is never read.
//
// NOT CLAIMED: `errno`, which error, or anything about the descriptors'
// lifetimes. `-1 | [0, MAX]` is the set {-1} ∪ [0, INT_MAX] (canonical
// `[-1, MAX]`).
//
// Deliberately NOT declared here: `timerfd_create` (Linux timerfd_create(2):
// a new descriptor, or -1), which epoll's timer arm reads. No pinned corpus
// unit declares it (`libc-names.txt`, the generated placement list, does not
// list it), so the placement test refuses it until that list is regenerated
// over a build that includes <sys/timerfd.h>; it is not on the channel
// chain. `kevent` (kqueue) and `evutil_socketpair` (libevent's) are read by
// no backend an audited build configures.

// POSIX.1-2017 pipe(): "Upon successful completion, 0 shall be returned;
// otherwise, -1 shall be returned and errno set to indicate the error."
// (`extern int pipe (int __pipedes[2]) __THROW __wur;`, <unistd.h>.)
//
// The written sets (card CELL-RESULT-SET-ALIGNMENT, grammar G05j as amended,
// gateway rule 38e as amended): on a return of 0, the descriptor `pipe`
// stored at `pipedes[0]` and at `pipedes[1]` is in [1, MAX].
//
// USER DECISION 2026-11-04 (verbatim): "Basically, Q1(a) and Q2(i) But we
// must not handle descriptor 0 as a valid handle. So, we need to exclude the
// 0 descriptor like: written_set(pipedes, [1, MAX]); a live descriptor is in
// [1, MAX]".
// USER DECISION 2026-11-04 (verbatim, after the counter-evidence below was
// put to the user): "Write [1, MAX]".
//
// THIS IS A DECLARED POLICY, NOT POSIX'S SET. POSIX allocates the lowest
// free descriptor, so `pipe` returns descriptor 0 whenever 0 is free:
// POSIX's written set is [0, MAX]. It was observed natively: started with
// standard input closed, Fluent Bit 046accf6 (and master 49592c4fd with the
// user's third patch) creates `config->ch_data` as `pipe2([0, 3])`
// (W43-DESC-FLB-CONFIG-DATA-PIPE-ZERO-GUARD; CELL-RESULT-SET-ALIGNMENT step-6
// traces, docs/reports/cell-result-set-alignment/). Under this declaration
// every reading that rests on it treats descriptor 0 as never live, so a
// `> 0` test's dead edge reads "absent"; where descriptor 0 is in fact a
// live end that reading is wrong. Every row it moves is attributed to this
// bound (follow-up CELL-RESULT-SET-DESCRIPTOR-ZERO-POLICY).
extern fn pipe(pipedes: ptr<mut, u8>) -> i32
contract {
    requires bounds_contract_v1;
    requires bounds_revision(flexible);
    ensures normal result_set(-1 | 0);
    ensures normal written_set(pipedes[0], [1, MAX]) when #result == 0;
    ensures normal written_set(pipedes[1], [1, MAX]) when #result == 0;
};

// Linux epoll_ctl(2), RETURN VALUE: "When successful, epoll_ctl() returns
// zero. When an error occurs, epoll_ctl() returns -1 and errno is set to
// indicate the error." (`extern int epoll_ctl (int __epfd, int __op, int
// __fd, struct epoll_event *__event) __THROW;`, <sys/epoll.h>.)
extern fn epoll_ctl(epfd: i32, op: i32, fd: i32, event: ptr<mut, u8>) -> i32
contract {
    requires bounds_contract_v1;
    requires bounds_revision(flexible);
    ensures normal result_set(-1 | 0);
};

// POSIX.1-2017 open(): "Upon successful completion, these functions shall
// open the file and return a non-negative integer representing the file
// descriptor. Otherwise, these functions shall return -1 and set errno to
// indicate the error." (`extern int open (const char *__file, int __oflag,
// ...) __nonnull ((1));`, <fcntl.h>.) The variadic `mode` is not a parameter
// of this declaration; a result set says nothing about any actual.
extern fn open(file: ptr<const, u8>, oflag: i32) -> i32
contract {
    requires bounds_contract_v1;
    requires bounds_revision(flexible);
    ensures normal result_set(-1 | [0, MAX]);
};
